-/// Implementation is taken from [std-detect][std-detect].
+/// Upstream reads the CPU feature bits with the `cpuid` instruction (plus
+/// `xgetbv` for the OS XSAVE state), which rustc emits as *Intel-dialect*
+/// inline assembly.  The Fil-Pizlonator only accepts AT&T dialect inline
+/// assembly, and the pizlonator's `cpuid` whitelist additionally requires
+/// every register `cpuid` writes (EAX/EBX/ECX/EDX) to be declared as an
+/// output or clobber -- which cannot be satisfied from Rust, because rustc
+/// refuses to name `ebx` as an inline-asm operand or clobber on x86_64
+/// ("rbx is used internally by LLVM and cannot be used as an operand for
+/// inline asm"), and the upstream mov/xchg scratch-register trick (which
+/// saves and restores `ebx` without declaring it) is rejected for the same
+/// reason.  libm is a `no_std` crate with no libc dependency, so unlike
+/// std_detect (which parses /proc/cpuinfo for the same reason) it also has
+/// no file-IO fallback.
