-/// [std-detect]: https://github.com/rust-lang/stdarch/blob/690b3a6334d482874163bd6fcef408e0518febe9/crates/std_detect/src/detect/os/x86.rs#L142
+/// Reporting no features is always safe: the dispatch in `fma.rs` then
+/// selects the portable software implementations, which are correct on
+/// every CPU (they are merely slower than the hardware-FMA ones).  Note
+/// that the `vfmadd*` inline-assembly bodies in `fma.rs` are therefore
+/// unreachable under Fil-C.
